Since the pervasion of mere effect-nature with mere creator-nature, like that of mere 'being-made' with mere impermanence in the case of a pot and the like, is established. Otherwise, if one were to posit different reasons based on different properties of the example and what is to be proved, there would be the absence of all inference whatsoever, since there is no difference [in principle]. But the paleness [of a substance] — since it is present even in the absence of smoke, in snow, <s>makkola</s>, and other [pale substances] — is indeed not suitable as an inferrer of fire.
Nor is the reason inconclusive, since everything without a [known] creator — even forest grass and the like — has been included in the subject (<s>pakṣa</s>). Nor is the reason contradictory, as the <s>Jaiminīyas</s> say:
'And if the example is thus unestablished, the reason would be contradictory;
